  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 153 PM CDT Wed Sep 16 2026\n\nFortunately for us, heat advisories look like they may be on a \nhiatus for the next few days. While moisture increases for Thursday, \ncloud cover and the potential for rain should limit temperatures \nand, thus, heat-related impacts. \n\n\nPWAT values will increase to near 2.2\" for Thursday, which could \nlead to some areas of heavy rainfall and localized flash flooding, \nparticularly if the storms are slow-movers. Increased moisture and a \nlow potential for rain will continue through Friday afternoon. Rain \nchances will drop to 5-20% by this weekend and into early next, with \nrain chances mainly along the seabreeze.\n\n\nModels show a long easterly fetch developing across the northern \ngulf waters this week which may help push water farther up the \nbeaches. Will continue to monitor trends for slightly higher than \nnormal tides and/or an increased rip current risk.  At this time, \nminor coastal flooding is not anticipated but will continue to be \nmonitored.",
